{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4652233","formula":"C₂₂H₂₇N₃O","hill":"C22H27N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"H":27.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"N-allylnorlysergic acid N,N-diethylamide","ru":"AL-LAD"},"descriptions":{"en":"AL-LAD, or ALLAD, also known as ALLY-LAD or as 6-allyl-6-nor-LSD, is a psychedelic drug of the lysergamide family related to lysergic acid diethylamide (LSD). It is taken orally. The drug interacts with serotonin and dopamine receptors and is known to act as an agonist of the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor similarly to LSD. AL-LAD produces psychedelic-like effects in animals.","ru":"AL-LAD, также известный как 6-аллил-6-нор-ЛСД, представляет собой психоделический препарат и структурный аналог диэтиламида лизергиновой кислоты (ЛСД). Он описан Александром Шульгиным в книге TiHKAL (Триптамины, которые я узнал и полюбил). Он синтезируется исходя из NO-LSD в качестве предшественника, используя аллилбромид в качестве реагента."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":15227511,"mass":349.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCN(CC)C(=O)[C@H]1CN([C@@H]2CC3=CNC4=CC=CC(=C34)C2=C1)CC=C","inchikey":"JCQLEPDZFXGHHQ-OXQOHEQNSA-N","iupac":"(6aR,9R)-N,N-diethyl-7-prop-2-enyl-6,6a,8,9-tetrahydro-4H-indolo[4,3-fg]quinoline-9-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"15227511","atoms":53,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.236,"y":1.981,"z":-1.221,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.501,"y":-1.823,"z":0.094,"el":"N"},{"x":5.333,"y":-0.427,"z":0.176,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.928,"y":1.252,"z":0.196,"el":"N"},{"x":0.789,"y":-1.178,"z":-0.281,"el":"C"},{"x":0.811,"y":0.354,"z":0.003,"el":"C"},{"x":1.976,"y":-1.949,"z":0.409,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.645,"y":0.343,"z":0.373,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.643,"y":-1.008,"z":-0.346,"el":"C"},{"x":3.249,"y":-1.192,"z":0.282,"el":"C"},{"x":2.115,"y":1.049,"